{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-252", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/252", "wordCount": 2315, "segments": [{"start": 7.0, "text": "Hi, this is Tom from the Car"}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "Experience Team at Apple and"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "welcome to our talk on Advances"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "in CarPlay Systems."}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "As you know, CarPlay is the"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "smarter, safer way to use your"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "iPhone in the car."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "iOS 13 has a ton of new updates"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "to CarPlay including the all-new"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "CarPlay Dashboard for a simple"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "view of your tunes, turns and"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "Smart Siri suggestions."}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "In this session we will"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "introduce you to vehicle"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "integration features newly"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "available in iOS 13."}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "All of the features we will talk"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "about today will require the"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "vehicle system to adopt new APIs"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "available in the CarPlay"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "Communication plug-in R15."}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "Today we will introduce new"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "display and audio features in"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "CarPlay that you can take"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "advantage of in future vehicles."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "First up, let's look at how"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "CarPlay supports irregularly"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "shaped displays."}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "The vehicle declares the"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "physical size and resolution of"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "the display and iPhone will"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "setup an H.264 video stream of"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "that size which will be rendered"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "to the display."}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "Prior to iOS 13, the CarPlay UI"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "would be drawn up to each edge"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "of the video screen."}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "However, some car displays are"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "fitted with pieces of trim that"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "may obscure parts of the CarPlay"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "user interface, restricting"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "access to some touchable"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "controls and preventing the user"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "from being able to see certain"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "parts of the UI."}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "With iOS 13, CarPlay now"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "supports irregularly shaped"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "displays."}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "First, your system defines a"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "view area."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "This represents the rectangle"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "that CarPlay can draw a user"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "interface image into."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "A view area can also contain a"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "safe area."}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "The safe area is also a"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "rectangular area and must be a"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "subset of the view area."}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "The safe area represents the"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "portion of the display that will"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "contain interactive content."}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "This includes user interface"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "elements such as buttons and"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "lists and important status"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "information like time, signal"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "strength and route guidance"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "iPhone will draw interactive"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "content within the boundaries of"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "the safe area."}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "Modern car displays can come in"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "many different shapes and sizes."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "Displays themselves may be"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "non-rectangular or portions of"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "the display may be occluded by"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "other elements."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "With iOS 13, CarPlay can use"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "safe areas to better support"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "non-rectangular shaped displays."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "First, the system defines a view"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "area."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "The view area rectangle in this"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "case would be made up of the"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "widest and tallest points of the"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "display."}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "This allows the CarPlay image to"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "render to all parts of the"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "display."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "Then a safe area rectangle will"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "be declared for the part of the"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "display where a CarPlay UI is"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "guaranteed to be visible and"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "interactable to the user."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "And that was our update on"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "irregularly shaped displays."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "Next up, let's talk about second"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "screen support in CarPlay."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "Prior to iOS 13, iPhone provided"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "a single H.264 video screen to"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "display the CarPlay UI on the"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "center console display."}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "This provides a great way for"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "users to set a navigation"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "destination, interact with music"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "apps and more."}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "However, this limits the user's"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "CarPlay experience to the"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "vehicle's main display."}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "Many vehicles have rich displays"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "directly in front of the driver"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "to show important information in"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "the form of an instrument"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "cluster."}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "In iOS 13, we now support"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "multiple H.264 video streams to"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "display CarPlay content in the"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "vehicle's instrument cluster."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "This is a great way to display"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "additional information from"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "CarPlay apps directly in the"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "instrument cluster."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "And different types of"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "information can be displayed in"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "different areas of the"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "instrument cluster using more"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "than one video stream."}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "In iOS 13, CarPlay will support"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "a maneuver instruction card"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "provided by Apple Maps, as well"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "as a map view which can be"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "rendered in parallel with the"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "instruction card in two separate"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "video streams."}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "Each video stream will have an"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "independent night mode, allowing"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "the vehicle system to specify an"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "appearance mode for different"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "content types."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "Also, the vehicle chooses what"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "type of content is shown in each"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "stream."}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "For instrument clusters, car"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "play will only draw the type of"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "content the vehicle has"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "selected. But please note for heads-up"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "displays, information from iAP2"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "Route Guidance will continue to"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "be used."}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "So with this in mind, let's look"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "at how to best utilize the"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "different available protocols to"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "integrate CarPlay into a vehicle"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "instrument cluster."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "Users can be provided with"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "simple status information from"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "apps in CarPlay such as"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "navigation, audio and phone"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "calls."}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "Firstly, map or turn-by-turn"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "information provided as a video"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "from iPhone can be displayed."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "Additional information about the"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "navigation route can also be"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "provided as metadata using the"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "iAP2 Route Guidance feature."}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "This, like other iAP2 features,"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "requires the vehicle to draw the"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "metadata in its own native UI."}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "The currently playing track or"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "podcasts can be rendered using"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "iAP2 Now Playing along with any"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "information about ongoing phone"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "calls using the iAP2"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "Communications feature."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "Control of those phone calls can"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "be supported using iAP2 Call"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "Controls, allowing the system to"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "offer specific user actions"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "during phone calls like mute,"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "swap call and end call."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "Displaying CarPlay content in"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "the instrument cluster is"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "another part of the vehicle"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "system that benefits from using"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "safe areas and view areas."}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "In this example, the view area"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "would be the rectangle between"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "and behind the virtual"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "tachometers."}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "While aesthetically it may be"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "desirable for CarPlay content to"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "fill this region, some of it"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "would be obscured by the virtual"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "tachometers."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "So a safe area would be declared"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "in the area between the two"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "tachometers and CarPlay will"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "position the important"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "information where it will be"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "visible to the user."}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "And multiple streams can be set"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "up to display different types of"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "content from CarPlay within the"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "instrument cluster."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "For example, the second stream"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "could be a map view and the"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "third stream an instruction"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "card."}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "Displaying content within a"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "virtual tachometer will also"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "make use of view areas and safe"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "areas."}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "The rectangle containing the"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "entire circle would be the view"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "area, and the rectangle"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "contained entirely within the"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "circle is the safe area."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "Again, CarPlay will position the"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "important information where it"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "will be visible to the user."}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "So that was our update on"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "support for second screens."}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "Now let's take a look at the"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "last of our new features that"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "affects displays in CarPlay,"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "dynamic screen resizing."}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "Prior to iOS 13, the size of the"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "CarPlay image remained fixed"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "while the CarPlay session was"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "active."}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "Now the size of the CarPlay UI"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "can change on the fly at the"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "user's request by declaring"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "multiple view areas for that"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "display."}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "This is ideal for systems that"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "support configurable horizontal"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "split screens as shown here, and"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "larger portrait screens that are"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "normally divided into distinct"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "context-specific regions."}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "CarPlay can provide an Always"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "Available button for the user to"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "trigger a resize request from"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "within the CarPlay UI."}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "This is useful to show CarPlay"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "in a full-screen configuration"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "without reserving space in the"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "native UI for dedicated control"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "for the user to exit that"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "configuration."}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "Resizing is not only supported"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "on the center console display"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "but also on the instrument"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "cluster as well."}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "So let's use the instrument"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "cluster from the previous"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "section as an example of how"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "dynamic resizing could be used"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "in CarPlay."}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "Let's say this instrument"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "cluster offers the user a way to"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "move the virtual tachometers"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "into one of two preferred"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "positions."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "For this to work well, the"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "CarPlay image needs to be able"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "to adjust its size based on"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "where the virtual tachometers"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "are positioned."}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "Multiple view areas can be"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "declared for this display to"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "make this happen."}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "Let's declare the first view"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "area for the widest"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "configuration and include a safe"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "area as discussed earlier."}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "For the narrower configuration,"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "a second view area would be used"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "with its own narrower safe area."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "The vehicle system can also"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "specify how long the transition"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "between those configurations"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "should take, allowing the"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "CarPlay content to transition"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "sizes in the same timeframe."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "Let's take a look at how this"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "transition would work."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "The user starts in the wider"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "configuration and uses some"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "native UI control, possibly a"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "steering wheel button, to begin"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "the transition."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "During this three-second transition, CarPlay is telling"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "the native system the size of"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "the encoded image in the H.264"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "frame, allowing the vehicle"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "system to synchronize the"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "position of its own tachometer"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "UI elements."}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "So in summary, dynamic resizing"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "is supported on center console"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "and instrument cluster displays."}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "A UI resize can be triggered by"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "the user either through the"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "native UI or a button within the"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "CarPlay UI."}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "The vehicle system declares how"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "long transitions between view"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "areas should take."}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "And CarPlay provides an update"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "on how far the view area"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "transition it is so the vehicle"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "system can synchronize"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "transition animations in its own"}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "UI."}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "So that's all for our new"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "display-related features."}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "Thanks for listening so far."}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "Now over to Tanya for an update"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "on Siri in CarPlay."}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "Thanks, Tom."}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "My name is Tanya Kancheva and"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "I'll talk to you about enabling"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "Hey Siri support in future"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "vehicles."}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "So what do we mean when we talk"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "about supporting Hey Siri in"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "your car?"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "First, of course, the driver can"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "launch Siri completely"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "hands-free without needing to"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "press a button or take their"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "eyes off the road."}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "And since Hey Siri is detected"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "using the car's microphone,"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "iPhone can be out of sight, left"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "in a pocket or even in the"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "trunk."}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "Siri will still be available."}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "We also updated audio handling"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "so that activating Siri through"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "a button press is instantaneous."}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "Just hold the Siri button on the"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "steering wheel and say your"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "request without waiting for an"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "audible trigger to speak."}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "Siri will be back with your"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "answer immediately."}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "Lastly, we looked at how Siri"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "and Music interplay in the car"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "and enable the smoother and more"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "familiar experience."}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "Music continues to play in the"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "background while interacting"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "with Siri."}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "Here is a system overview for"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "audio handling in CarPlay."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "Some of the components should"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "already be familiar to you, but"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "let's go ahead and look into the"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "details."}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "To support Hey Siri, the in-car"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "microphone needs to be always"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "active and undergo continuous"}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "voice processing."}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "The echo cancellation module"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "runs all the time and removes"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "any audio playing through the"}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "car's speakers as well as"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "reduces background driving"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "noise."}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "The process microphone data is"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "sent to an audio ring buffer"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "within the CarPlay communication"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "plug-in which holds a couple of"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "seconds of historical audio."}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "This buffer is stored within the"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "car until there is a trigger to"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "send it to iPhone."}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "So what is this trigger?"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "In fact, there are two modules"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "which can lead to audio exchange"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "with iPhone."}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "Both constantly analyze the"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "process microphone data."}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "One can trigger when the drive"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "says Siri."}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "That's the keyword detector."}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "The other one triggers when the"}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "drive starts talking."}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "That's the voice activity"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "detector."}, {"start": 709.0, "text": "Both detectors must be available"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "in the car as iPhone determines"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "which one is used for a"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "particular scenario."}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "Now let's say the keyword"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "detector triggered so the car"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "notifies iPhone through the"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "communication plug-in."}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "iPhone opens a new audio stream"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "called Aux In, requesting some"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "historical audio data to be"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "sent."}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "The received audio is reanalyzed"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "by a voice trigger detector on"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "iPhone which verifies that the"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "user said, \"Hey, Siri.\""}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "The second pass detector uses"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "offline keyword detection on"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "iPhone similar to how Hey Siri"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "is detected when the user is not"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "driving."}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "Only after the second pass"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "detector on iPhone triggers Siri"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "is activated to process the data"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "and respond to the user."}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "Now, let's look at how this"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "architecture is helping us"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "improve triggering Siri with a"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "button press."}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "As we already saw, the mic, the"}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "ECNR unit and the audio ring"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "buffer are processing audio"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "within the car system all the"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "time."}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "Now the user presses the Siri"}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "button on the steering wheel"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "that is the trigger for iPhone"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "to request audio data from the"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "time when the user pressed the"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "Since this is the button press,"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "Siri activates immediately."}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "And as the buffered audio is"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "sent faster than real-time, Siri"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "can be ready with a response"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "right after the user stops"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "talking."}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "Okay, now that we have discussed"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "the three ways in which Siri can"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "trigger from the car through a"}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "detected keyword, voice activity"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "or a button press, let's see"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "what happens when Siri is active"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "and helping the driver."}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "Typically, music will be playing"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "in the car."}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "In this case, let's say that"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "music is coming from iPhone."}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "The car will receive the audio,"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "mix it and play it through the"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "speakers."}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "In the past, when Siri started"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "in CarPlay, music had to stop"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "and there was a bit of silence"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "before Siri prompts played."}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "With this new architecture,"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "media playback is separated from"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "Siri prompts so the music can"}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "keep playing in the background."}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "When Siri launches, an"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "additional audio stream"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "dedicated to Siri output, Aux"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "Out, will be opened."}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "The car will then mix the two"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "streams, reduce the volume of"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "the music as needed and play"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "Siri prompts quickly and without"}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "big interruptions."}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "But please don't forget that in"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "addition to Siri prompts, there"}, {"start": 887.0, "text": "might be active route guidance,"}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "so the mixer has to be able to"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "mix three parallel audio streams"}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "coming from iPhone."}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "Now that we have gone through"}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "the details of the audio"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "architecture, let's quickly"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "summarize what is needed within"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "the vehicle system."}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "First, a microphone which is"}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "always processing audio in your"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "system."}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "Then, an echo canceller and"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "noise reduction module to clean"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "up microphone input."}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "A detector that triggers when"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "the driver is talking."}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "A detector that triggers when"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "the Siri keyword is heard."}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "The ability to mix three audio"}, {"start": 932.0, "text": "streams from CarPlay."}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "And that's how our update on Hey"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "Siri."}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "Thank you for your time."}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "For more information, check out"}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "developer.apple.com."}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "And enjoy your drive with"}]}
